<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! PoC 0: A source without a known camera

A user-authored oblique Necrospire RGBA and an independently archived L8
alpha supply the minimal testimony. A fixed provisional camera permits
repeatable silhouette comparison but cannot certify physical dimensions or
perspective. The source RGBA and alpha agree at every pixel (1024×1536).
The alpha source bears SHA-256
`78f8d1f0cf44a98b748054ae8b5c8f2229c1354696a8e1173963a7c98bc4fbe7`.
The RGBA bears SHA-256
`80e1d0ee8ae4bda505c053b42ea1d1f661d71ed4c174f57c15423027872c4f89`.

A location-wide, five-epoch full-speed constructive run selected four
CAD-valid survivors from scored proposals, keeping valid geometry and its
witness distinct from the model's drawings. All currently share a narrow
fortress/needle topology, even though dimensions vary. That limited diversity
reads as a constructive-grammar ceiling, not as measurement certainty.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/operator-and-model>>

!! Two pilots at one helm

* The Operator–AI pair MAY steer via the persistent OODA-HA inbox without any
  configured remote provider. Operator pet-names, o-takiage, reviews, pause and
  lineage choice remain phase-boundary actions with real receipts.
* A provider-backed adviser MAY connect Ollama (local) or an explicitly trusted
  OpenAI-compatible HTTP(S) chat endpoint. The model sees small classified
  summaries, not the original pixels, local secrets, full files, or arbitrary
  filesystem paths. Model replies are parsed and constrained to a reviewed
  candidate ID, an inquiry question, or abstention.
* Provider output never receives authority to certify a mesh, override CAD
  validity, invent survey ground control, or rewrite an existing source.
* Operator and model can change their desired degree of steering; no mode
  weakens source, camera, lineage, or strict CAD gates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/hard-reference-talk-story>>

!! The hard-reference fork remains open at the Operator's hand

A Penn Museum/Lagash photogrammetric Ziggurat of Ur offers source-authenticated
Sumerian terrain/terrace architecture with CC BY-NC use conditions. A CC0
OpenSCAD/STL brutalist architecture kit offers a compact executable reference
and distinct reconstructive method. A CC BY scanned megalithic passage tomb
at Øm offers a stronger interior void-and-circulation test. No source scan
becomes a watertight CAD model by declaration. Research links and licenses
live in the project's hard-reference scout; the final two await an operator
choice of method diversity versus architectural/circulation diversity.

<<~/ahu>>

